; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Barnsley Fern
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Advanced
; TAGS:     IFS, random, probability, DOT, affine maps, data tables
; SUMMARY:  Paints Michael Barnsley's fern with 20000 dots placed by four random rules.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Four simple rules each move a point: one makes the stem, one
;   makes the next smaller copy of the whole fern, and two make the
;   lowest left and right leaflets. Picking one rule at random again
;   and again (some more often than others) and putting a dot at
;   every new point paints a fern that looks almost real.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch the fern appear. The rules are a table in
;   SETUP.RULES; change a number and run again.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * an iterated function system (IFS)
;   * rules as data: each rule is a list of seven numbers
;   * choosing with given chances: RANDOM 100 and running totals
;   * scaling math coordinates to screen coordinates
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Change the 85 in the main rule to 75. The fern gets shorter.
;   * Change the 0.04 in the main rule to -0.04 so it bends the
;     other way.
;   * Color the dots by which rule made them.
; ============================================================

; Each rule is [a b c d e f chance]. It moves the point (x, y) to
;   new x = a x + b y + e
;   new y = c x + d y + f
; and is used chance times out of 100.
to setup.rules
  make "rules [
    [0     0     0     0.16  0  0     1]
    [0.85  0.04 -0.04  0.85  0  1.6   85]
    [0.2  -0.26  0.23  0.22  0  1.6   7]
    [-0.15 0.28  0.26  0.24  0  0.44  7]
  ]
end

; CHOOSE.RULE throws a 100 sided die and walks the table, adding up
; the chances until the total passes the throw.
to choose.rule
  localmake "throw random 100
  localmake "total 0
  foreach :rules [
    make "total :total + item 7 ?
    if :throw < :total [output ?]
  ]
  output last :rules
end

; APPLY.RULE changes the global point :x :y using one rule.
to apply.rule :r
  localmake "nx (item 1 :r) * :x + (item 2 :r) * :y + item 5 :r
  make "y (item 3 :r) * :x + (item 4 :r) * :y + item 6 :r
  make "x :nx
end

; PAINT plays the game :n times. The fern lives between x = -2.2
; and 2.7 and between y = 0 and 10, so it is scaled by 56 and moved
; down to fit the screen.
to paint :n
  make "x 0
  make "y 0
  repeat :n [
    apply.rule choose.rule
    ; Higher dots are a little lighter, like new growth.
    setpencolor (list 20 + 6 * :y 110 + 12 * :y 40)
    dot list 56 * :x 56 * :y - 285
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [12 20 16]
setpensize 1.5
setup.rules
paint 20000
